Possible spoilers:


After doing (of attempting to do) quests for 6 different character
classes, I would say, that the quests should be a bit better balanced.
Some are almost too easy for character after reaching the required 14-th
level, some are not... Yesterday I tried a priest quest and it killed me
in the end - the quest nemesis (whatever his name) is almost as powerful
as the wizard (more powerful than demon lords)! Archeologist or Valkyrie
quests were just walks compared to that. Also, the priest quest has a
completely unreasonable number of enemies in it - I lost more than one
evening to hack through them. The idea is very nice - but it needs some
tuning.

A byproduct of large number of monsters in the quests, the players
tend to pile unresonable amuonts of equipment. I think 'less-monsters-but-
more-demanding' quests would be much nicer.

Btw: Somebody complained, that neutrals do not have an artifact to
protect from level drains. No artifact, but they have a way...
(more spoiler)


During the priest quest I noticed, that I was immune to level drains, but
only until a succubus has stripped me naked... Later I checked in wizard 
mode all pieces of armor I had - and found that an elven mithril-coat was
apparently giving me the immunity. I'm wondering what other armor could have
some hidden properties?

